            {
                "question": "What is LinkCoin?",
                "answer": "LinkCoin is a peer-to-peer cryptocurrency network established in 2014. It utilizes the scrypt Proof-of-Work algorithm."
            },
            {
                "question": "Who represents LinkCoin?",
                "answer": "No one. LinkCoin does not have a CEO, foundation, or official marketing team. It is maintained by independent individuals."
            },
            {
                "question": "Is development active?",
                "answer": "The protocol is stable (legacy). Maintenance is performed by community volunteers as needed to ensure compatibility and node functionality."
            },
            {
                "question": "How does mining work?",
                "answer": "LinkCoin can be mined using scrypt-compatible hardware. It supports merge-mining with other scrypt-based chains."
            }
        ],
